# strong(...) over an unbounded sequence is a liveness obligation; the weak
# monitors (register v3 D2) must not compile it: a precise refusal.  The
# response form `ant |-> strong(##[m:$] R)` is lowered as a temporal
# response since fe21 (sva_strong_response.ys); other shapes stay refused.
logger -expect error "strong unbounded sequence in .* needs a liveness obligation" 1
read_verilog -sv -formal <<EOT
module top (input logic clk, input logic a, input logic b);
  p: assert property (@(posedge clk) strong(a ##[1:$] b));
endmodule
EOT
prep -top top
sva2check
